   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *          functionalities of the Inter-integrated circuit (I2C)
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *           + Data transfers
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *           + PEC management
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *           + DMA transfers management
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *           + Interrupts, events and flags management 
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *           
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     @verbatim    
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  ===============================================================================
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                     ##### How to use this driver #####
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  ===============================================================================
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     [..]
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Enable peripheral clock using RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_I2Cx, ENABLE)
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           function for I2C1, I2C2 or I2C3.
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Enable SDA, SCL  and SMBA (when used) GPIO clocks using 
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           RCC_AHBPeriphClockCmd() function. 
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Peripherals alternate function: 
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Connect the pin to the desired peripherals' Alternate 
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              Function (AF) using GPIO_PinAFConfig() function
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Configure the desired pin in alternate function by:
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccKogwsQ.s 			page 2


  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              GPIO_InitStruct->GPIO_Mode = GPIO_Mode_AF
  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Select the type, pull-up/pull-down and output speed via 
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              GPIO_PuPd, GPIO_OType and GPIO_Speed members
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Call GPIO_Init() function
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              Recommended configuration is Push-Pull, Pull-up, Open-Drain.
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              Add an external pull up if necessary (typically 4.7 KOhm).      
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Program the Mode, duty cycle , Own address, Ack, Speed and Acknowledged
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           Address using the I2C_Init() function.
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Optionally you can enable/configure the following parameters without
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           re-initialization (i.e there is no need to call again I2C_Init() function):
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Enable the acknowledge feature using I2C_AcknowledgeConfig() function
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Enable the dual addressing mode using I2C_DualAddressCmd() function
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Enable the general call using the I2C_GeneralCallCmd() function
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Enable the clock stretching using I2C_StretchClockCmd() function
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Enable the fast mode duty cycle using the I2C_FastModeDutyCycleConfig()
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              function.
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Configure the NACK position for Master Receiver mode in case of 
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              2 bytes reception using the function I2C_NACKPositionConfig().  
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Enable the PEC Calculation using I2C_CalculatePEC() function
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) For SMBus Mode: 
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (+++) Enable the Address Resolution Protocol (ARP) using I2C_ARPCmd() function
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (+++) Configure the SMBusAlert pin using I2C_SMBusAlertConfig() function
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Enable the NVIC and the corresponding interrupt using the function 
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           I2C_ITConfig() if you need to use interrupt mode. 
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) When using the DMA mode 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Configure the DMA using DMA_Init() function
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (++) Active the needed channel Request using I2C_DMACmd() or
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              I2C_DMALastTransferCmd() function.
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         -@@- When using DMA mode, I2C interrupts may be used at the same time to
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              control the communication flow (Start/Stop/Ack... events and errors).
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****    
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Enable the I2C using the I2C_Cmd() function.
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****    
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       (#) Enable the DMA using the DMA_Cmd() function when using DMA mode in the 
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           transfers. 
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     @endverbatim  
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   ******************************************************************************
