 646:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @brief  Selects the specified I2C NACK position in master receiver mode.
 647:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @note   This function is useful in I2C Master Receiver mode when the number
 648:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *         of data to be received is equal to 2. In this case, this function 
 649:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *         should be called (with parameter I2C_NACKPosition_Next) before data 
 650:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *         reception starts,as described in the 2-byte reception procedure 
 651:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *         recommended in Reference Manual in Section: Master receiver.                
 652:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @param  I2Cx: where x can be 1, 2 or 3 to select the I2C peripheral.
 653:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @param  I2C_NACKPosition: specifies the NACK position. 
 654:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *          This parameter can be one of the following values:
 655:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *            @arg I2C_NACKPosition_Next: indicates that the next byte will be the last
 656:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *                                        received byte.  
 657:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *            @arg I2C_NACKPosition_Current: indicates that current byte is the last 
 658:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *                                           received byte.
 659:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *            
 660:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   * @note    This function configures the same bit (POS) as I2C_PECPositionConfig() 
 661:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *          but is intended to be used in I2C mode while I2C_PECPositionConfig() 
 662:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *          is intended to used in SMBUS mode. 
 663:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****   *            
