 955:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** /** @defgroup I2C_Group5 Interrupts events and flags management functions
 956:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  *  @brief   Interrupts, events and flags management functions
 957:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  *
 958:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** @verbatim   
 959:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  ===============================================================================
 960:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           ##### Interrupts, events and flags management functions #####
 961:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  ===============================================================================
 962:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     [..]
 963:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     This section provides functions allowing to configure the I2C Interrupts 
 964:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     sources and check or clear the flags or pending bits status.
 965:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     The user should identify which mode will be used in his application to manage 
 966:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     the communication: Polling mode, Interrupt mode or DMA mode. 
 967:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
 968:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
 969:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                 ##### I2C State Monitoring Functions #####                   
 970:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  =============================================================================== 
 971:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     [..]  
 972:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     This I2C driver provides three different ways for I2C state monitoring
 973:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****     depending on the application requirements and constraints:
 974:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****          
 975:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****    
 976:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****      (#) Basic state monitoring (Using I2C_CheckEvent() function)
 977:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****      
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccKogwsQ.s 			page 42


 978:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         It compares the status registers (SR1 and SR2) content to a given event
 979:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (can be the combination of one or more flags).
 980:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         It returns SUCCESS if the current status includes the given flags 
 981:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         and returns ERROR if one or more flags are missing in the current status.
 982:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
 983:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (++) When to use
 984:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) This function is suitable for most applications as well as for startup 
 985:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                activity since the events are fully described in the product reference 
 986:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                manual (RM0090).
 987:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) It is also suitable for users who need to define their own events.
 988:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
 989:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (++) Limitations
 990:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                If an error occurs (ie. error flags are set besides to the monitored 
 991:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                flags), the I2C_CheckEvent() function may return SUCCESS despite 
 992:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                the communication hold or corrupted real state. 
 993:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                In this case, it is advised to use error interrupts to monitor 
 994:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                the error events and handle them in the interrupt IRQ handler.
 995:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****          
 996:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****      -@@- For error management, it is advised to use the following functions:
 997:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (+@@) I2C_ITConfig() to configure and enable the error interrupts (I2C_IT_ERR).
 998:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (+@@) I2Cx_ER_IRQHandler() which is called when the error interrupt occurs.
 999:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****               Where x is the peripheral instance (I2C1, I2C2 ...)
1000:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (+@@) I2C_GetFlagStatus() or I2C_GetITStatus()  to be called into the 
1001:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****               I2Cx_ER_IRQHandler() function in order to determine which error occurred.
1002:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         (+@@) I2C_ClearFlag() or I2C_ClearITPendingBit() and/or I2C_SoftwareResetCmd() 
1003:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****               and/or I2C_GenerateStop() in order to clear the error flag and source 
1004:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****               and return to correct  communication status.
1005:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              
1006:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  
1007:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****      (#) Advanced state monitoring (Using the function I2C_GetLastEvent())
1008:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
1009:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         Using the function I2C_GetLastEvent() which returns the image of both status 
1010:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         registers in a single word (uint32_t) (Status Register 2 value is shifted left 
1011:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****         by 16 bits and concatenated to Status Register 1).
1012:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
1013:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (++) When to use
1014:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) This function is suitable for the same applications above but it 
1015:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                allows to overcome the mentioned limitation of I2C_GetFlagStatus() 
1016:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                function.
1017:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) The returned value could be compared to events already defined in 
1018:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                the library (stm32f4xx_i2c.h) or to custom values defined by user.
1019:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                This function is suitable when multiple flags are monitored at the 
1020:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                same time.
1021:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) At the opposite of I2C_CheckEvent() function, this function allows 
1022:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                user to choose when an event is accepted (when all events flags are 
1023:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                set and no other flags are set or just when the needed flags are set 
1024:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                like I2C_CheckEvent() function.
1025:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
1026:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (++) Limitations
1027:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) User may need to define his own events.
1028:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) Same remark concerning the error management is applicable for this 
1029:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                function if user decides to check only regular communication flags 
1030:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                (and ignores error flags).
1031:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       
1032:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  
1033:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****      (#) Flag-based state monitoring (Using the function I2C_GetFlagStatus())
1034:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****      
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccKogwsQ.s 			page 43


1035:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       Using the function I2C_GetFlagStatus() which simply returns the status of 
1036:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****       one single flag (ie. I2C_FLAG_RXNE ...). 
1037:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c **** 
1038:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (++) When to use
1039:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) This function could be used for specific applications or in debug 
1040:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                phase.
1041:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) It is suitable when only one flag checking is needed (most I2C 
1042:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                events are monitored through multiple flags).
1043:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****           (++) Limitations: 
1044:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) When calling this function, the Status register is accessed. 
1045:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                Some flags are cleared when the status register is accessed. 
1046:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                So checking the status of one Flag, may clear other ones.
1047:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****              (+++) Function may need to be called twice or more in order to monitor 
1048:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****                one single event.
1049:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****  
1050:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****    For detailed description of Events, please refer to section I2C_Events in 
1051:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****    stm32f4xx_i2c.h file.
1052:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_i2c.c ****        
